    {
      "text": "It hefts a Graveler repeatedly to strengthen its entire body. It uses every type of martial arts.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its whole body is composed of muscles. Even though it’s the size of a human child, it can hurl 100 grown-ups.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Machop’s muscles are special—they never get sore no matter how much they are used in exercise. This Pokémon has sufficient power to hurl a hundred adult humans.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Machop exercises by hefting around a Graveler as if it were a barbell. There are some Machop that travel the world in a quest to master all kinds of martial arts.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves working out. As it gazes at its muscles, which continue to swell day by day, it becomes more and more dedicated to its training.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its superhuman strength, it’s able to throw a hundred people all at the same time. Its strength comes from lifting Graveler every day.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once this Pokémon has gained enough confidence and muscle from training with its friends, it challenges Makuhita to a battle.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It likes food that’s highly nutritious because its instincts drive it to build muscle efficiently.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very powerful in spite of its small size. Its mastery of many types of martial arts makes it very tough.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very powerful in spite of its small size. Its mastery of many types of martial arts makes it very tough.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its whole body is composed of muscles. Even though it’s the size of a human child, it can hurl 100 grown-ups.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Always brimming with power, it passes time by lifting boulders. Doing so makes it even stronger.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Though as small as a child, it has strength enough to easily throw a well-built adult. Striving to become ever stronger, Machop trains by carrying a Graveler on its shoulders.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
